## SQ-FFH-02 | CD.food recipe ids (the 2026-10-26 dump diff half is stale: s3_skip.md)
@group B
@commands Rewritten 2026-10-27 (callers moved to `global.CD.food`, creative_delight.md 30); the 2026-10-27 CD jar is installed and in 1.1.04, so this is the dump diff only: boot, `/dumpall`, then diff the recipe dump against the 2026-10-26 one
@pass No `cd_food.js` or `global.CD.food` error in `logs/latest.log`. Every `creativedelight:baking/` id and the muffin `farmersdelightcooking/` ids unchanged; new: `farmersdelightcutting/<meat>_from_culture_<x>` (7, replacing `culture_*_by_fdcutting`) and `{smelting,smoking,campfirecooking}/cooked_calamari[_slice]_from_glowing_calamari[_slice]` (6, replacing `cooked_glowing_calamari*`); one Cooking Pot muffin recipe per muffin (no duplicate id error); nothing else gone
@fails Depends on: CD jar; creative_delight.md 30
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A.qb
@reviewed 2026-11-16
kjsreject (?i)(cd_food\.js|global\.CD\.food|CD\.food).*(error|exception)
bootreject (?i)duplicate recipe.*muffin
> cdevtest recipes creativedelight:baking/
> cdevtest recipes _from_culture_
> cdevtest recipes _by_fdcutting
> cdevtest recipes _from_glowing_calamari
> cdevtest recipes cooked_glowing_calamari
> cdevtest recipes muffin
expect verb=recipes text=creativedelight:baking/ n=[1-9]
count verb=recipes id=creativedelight:farmersdelightcutting/[a-z_]+_from_culture_\S* result= == 7
reject verb=recipes id=\S*culture_\S*_by_fdcutting
count verb=recipes id=\S*(smelting|smoking|campfirecooking)/cooked_calamari(_slice)?_from_glowing_calamari(_slice)? result= == 6
expect verb=recipes text=cooked_glowing_calamari n=0\b
look muffin lines: one farmersdelightcooking/ (Cooking Pot) recipe per muffin
reject \[cdevtest\] verb=\S+ .*error=

